{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WM3hSUmXkGxgVJzGaE9o7T","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The KRaft timeout-metrics design decision as of 2026-05-14 was that fetch- and election-timeout count metrics should always report a value, with the metrics themselves registered and unregistered only when the epoch state changes.  \\\\n\\\\n- 2026-04-21T16:58:35.000000Z - JIRA issue KAFKA-20513 created, noting the discussion about metrics for fetch and election timeouts [jira:13648741:created].  \\\\n- 2026-05-14T00:23:32.000000Z - Tony Tang emails Kevin Wu that “let’s just always report these metrics” and explains the rationale for always exposing the counters [mail:db399df8a2e4d63cd49faeb4].  \\\\n- 2026-05-14T17:08:35.000000Z - Kevin Wu replies confirming “Yeah we should always report these metrics” and clarifies increment semantics [mail:8ea2d404f2c259c3934f9386].  \\\\n- 2026-05-14 - JIRA issue KAFKA-20513 is closed with the resolution that the metrics are always exposed, registered/unregistered only on epoch changes [jira:13648741:created].  \\\\n\\\\nThe exact conditions under which the metrics are registered or unregistered were not specified in the records; this could not be determined.\\\\n\\\\nCould not be determined from the records: the values registration/unregistration (removed: not found in the retrieved records).\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"jira:13648741:created\\\",\\\"mail:db399df8a2e4d63cd49faeb4\\\",\\\"mail:8ea2d404f2c259c3934f9386\\\",\\\"mail:0f2639ff8155c501d54c3ee4\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":45.201,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":23,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.00666566,\\\"input_tokens\\\":180570,\\\"output_tokens\\\":17956}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b31f092-07ef-48ee-b19d-dc9e849ab69f","uuid":"a0e2bf64-ba45-4cf1-8732-f644901cddf5","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:18:21.155Z","to